      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <arm_neon.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    float *best_dist = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n    char *best_label = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n\n    int count = 0;\n    int i, j, t;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        // Process points in batches of four using NEON\n        for (j = 0; j + 3 < g.length; j += 4) {\n            float32x4x2_t pts = vld2q_f32((const float32_t *)&g.points[j]);\n            float32x4_t xs = pts.val[0];\n            float32x4_t ys = pts.val[1];\n            float32x4_t qx = vdupq_n_f32(to_evaluate.x);\n            float32x4_t qy = vdupq_n_f32(to_evaluate.y);\n            float32x4_t dx = xs - qx;\n            float32x4_t dy = ys - qy;\n            float32x4_t d2 = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n            float d[4];\n            vst1q_f32(d, d2);\n\n            for (t = 0; t < 4; t++) {\n                float dist_val = d[t];\n                if (count < k) {\n                    int pos = count;\n                    best_dist[pos] = dist_val;\n                    best_label[pos] = g.label;\n                    while (pos > 0 && best_dist[pos - 1] > dist_val) {\n                        float tmpd = best_dist[pos - 1];\n                        best_dist[pos - 1] = best_dist[pos];\n                        best_dist[pos] = tmpd;\n                        char tmpl = best_label[pos - 1];\n                        best_label[pos - 1] = best_label[pos];\n                        best_label[pos] = tmpl;\n                        pos--;\n                    }\n                    count++;\n                } else if (dist_val < best_dist[k - 1]) {\n                    int pos = k - 1;\n                    best_dist[pos] = dist_val;\n                    best_label[pos] = g.label;\n                    while (pos > 0 && best_dist[pos - 1] > best_dist[pos]) {\n                        float tmpd = best_dist[pos - 1];\n                        best_dist[pos - 1] = best_dist[pos];\n                        best_dist[pos] = tmpd;\n                        char tmpl = best_label[pos - 1];\n                        best_label[pos - 1] = best_label[pos];\n                        best_label[pos] = tmpl;\n                        pos--;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Scalar remainder\n        for (; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float dist_val = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n            if (count < k) {\n                int pos = count;\n                best_dist[pos] = dist_val;\n                best_label[pos] = g.label;\n                while (pos > 0 && best_dist[pos - 1] > dist_val) {\n                    float tmpd = best_dist[pos - 1];\n                    best_dist[pos - 1] = best_dist[pos];\n                    best_dist[pos] = tmpd;\n                    char tmpl = best_label[pos - 1];\n                    best_label[pos - 1] = best_label[pos];\n                    best_label[pos] = tmpl;\n                    pos--;\n                }\n                count++;\n            } else if (dist_val < best_dist[k - 1]) {\n                int pos = k - 1;\n                best_dist[pos] = dist_val;\n                best_label[pos] = g.label;\n                while (pos > 0 && best_dist[pos - 1] > best_dist[pos]) {\n                    float tmpd = best_dist[pos - 1];\n                    best_dist[pos - 1] = best_dist[pos];\n                    best_dist[pos] = tmpd;\n                    char tmpl = best_label[pos - 1];\n                    best_label[pos - 1] = best_label[pos];\n                    best_label[pos] = tmpl;\n                    pos--;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Count frequencies among the k selected labels\n    char *labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * count);\n    for (i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n        labels[i] = best_label[i];\n    }\n    qsort(labels, count, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (i = 1; i < count; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == count - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(best_dist);\n    free(best_label);\n    free(labels);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing the heap-based top-k selection with a fixed-size sorted array using insertion sort reduces per-point branch overhead and improves cache locality for small k, while retaining NEON SIMD distance computation; this should outperform the max-heap variant on typical benchmark inputs.",
  "notes": "The new implementation keeps the NEON batch distance calculation but replaces the heap (with its sift_up/sift_down functions) by a simple sorted array of size k. Insertion uses strict greater-than comparisons, so ties preserve first-come order exactly as in the reference. The frequency counting now operates only on actually filled entries, avoiding artificial -1 labels when fewer than k points exist.",
